\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Bk Indonesia Surprises By Keeping Rates Steady  \b0\par\par\uc2 843 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Januar 2006\par 11:36\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    (Updates with analysts' comments, closing rupiah price) \par  \par    By I Made Sentana and Phelim Kyne \par    OF DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--Bank Indonesia's board of governors decided at a policy meeting Monday to leave the one-month benchmark rate unchanged at 12.75%, surprising traders and analysts, who had expected an interest-rate rise.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cited a rising \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stable inflation for the lack of action, which follows interest-rate increases at every prior policy meeting since last July.  \par \par \uc2 "The rate hasn't increased due to the latest developments in the economy where inflation is under control and the rupiah is on a rising trend," Bank Indonesia Deputy Governor Aslim Tadjuddin later told reporters.  \par \par \uc2 "The decision not to hike the rate is expected to keep the macroeconomy stable and create a conducive climate for growth," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Still, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will maintain its tight monetary policy, Tadjuddin said.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts had predicted that Bank Indonesia would raise rates following a 175-basis-point increase in its benchmark rate since November, to address lingering inflationary pressure powered by the government's move to, on average, more than double fuel prices last October.  \par \par \uc2 But a slowing in inflation in December likely emboldened the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slightly loosen their recent tight monetary policy footing, said CIMB-GK Research Pte. Ltd. vice president of regional economics, Song Seng Wun.  \par \par \uc2 "The fact that the December consumer price index fell probably gave them a little bit more confidence (to temporarily halt rate hikes)," Song said.  \par \par \uc2 "They are also well aware that the spike in rates has affected the economy...so they're balancing what they have to do on the inflation-control front and what they need for the broader economy," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Indonesia's on-year inflation slowed to 17.11% in December from 18.38% in November. The country recorded 0.04% on-month deflation in December after 1.31% inflation in November.  \par \par \uc2 Inflationary Pressure, Rates To Steadily Decline  \par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia officials have routinely warned that they will keep a tight grip on the monetary policy levers, and analysts had predicted that the benchmark rate could rise to around 14.0% by mid-2006.  \par \par \uc2 The government of President Susilo Bambang Yudhoyono has cautioned that a combination of accelerated government spending, pending price hikes for public utilities and a 15.0% on-year salary increase for civil servants will continue to feed inflationary pressure in 2006.  \par \par \uc2 But December's data foreshadows an easing in inflation, which will prompt Bank Indonesia to scale back its tightening policy, Deutsche Bank said in a research note before the latest policy decision.  \par \par \uc2 "The inflation rate is likely to creep lower over the next two quarters, and then drop sharply in October as last year's fuel prices drop out of the calculation," the report said. "We expect Bank Indonesia will raise interest rates only a little over the next two quarters, perhaps keeping pace with the Fed, but then lower interest rates sharply in the fourth quarter."  \par \par \uc2 The end-2006 rate cut could "easily be much more" than 100 basis points, Deutsche Bank said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been trying to carefully calibrate its anti-inflation rate hike policy so that it doesn't smother consumer consumption, which makes up around 70.0% of annual gross domestic product. The government has projected GDP expansion of 6.2% in 2006, outpacing the projected 6.0% rise in 2005.  \par \par \uc2 "They need to give the local economy a little bit of a break (in terms of lower rates) or that GDP target will be quite difficult to achieve," Song said.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Unlikely To \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  In \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Market  \par \par \uc2 The decision to keep rates steady came as the U.S. dollar continued to slide against Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The dollar closed Monday at IDR9,455, from IDR9,570 Friday and after touching an eight-month low of IDR9,430 in early trading.  \par \par \uc2 Central banks across Asia closely watched the dollar's continuing fall against a broad range of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and traders suspect a number have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow the greenback's fall.  \par \par \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Tadjuddin said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves its right to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, but he indicated that such action was unlikely in the short term.  \par \par \uc2 "In terms of keeping the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market stable, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is always open...(but) what the ideal value of the rupiah is, we leave it to the market," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Tadjuddin attributed the rupiah's current strength to short-term foreign capital inflow on expectations that Indonesia's economy would continue to improve and he said the rupiah's rise against the dollar would help curb inflation.  \par \par \uc2 That view was echoed by Standard Chartered economist Fauzi Ichsan.  \par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia's move to not hike rates Monday "won't hurt the rupiah", Ichsan said.  \par \par \uc2 -By I Made Sentana and Phelim Kyne; Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21-39893-1277; I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Iain McDonald [ 09-01-06 1036GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060109e219000l2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
