\par\par \b \uc2 Indonesia Rupiah Ends Up On Dlr Weakness, Stocks Rally  \b0\par\par\uc2 487 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Januar 2006\par 11:25\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The Indonesian rupiah ended at a nearly eight-month high Monday due to the dollar's tumble against most regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and strong capital inflows to the stock market, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar closed at IDR9,455 versus IDR9,570 Friday. Monday's close is the dollar's lowest since May 23 when it ended at IDR9,445.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar lost ground against most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday because of weaker-than expected U.S. jobs data.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the influx of capital to the Indonesian market, which yet rose to another record high Monday also helped the rupiah. The Jakarta Stock Exchange Composite Index rose 1.9% Monday to 1,245.054 points.  \par \par \uc2 The rupiah's nearly 4% gains so far this year and easing inflation in December prompted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep its key one-month rate unchanged at 12.75% Monday. Many analysts had expected another 25-basis point hike.  \par \par \uc2 "The rate hasn't increased due to the latest developments in the economy where inflation is under control and the rupiah is on a rising trend," Bank Indonesia deputy governor Aslim Tadjuddin told reporters. "The decision not to hike the rate is expected to keep the macroeconomy stable and create a conducive climate for growth," he said.  \par \par \uc2 However, he added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will maintain its tight monetary policy. Many analysts are still expecting a gentle rate hike during the first half of the year.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was widely unfazed by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to keep rates unchanged as the move is expected to further lift sentiment in the local stock and bond markets, which should then benefit the rupiah.  \par \par \uc2 "The contribution of the stock rise to the rupiah's recent gains is quite significant," said Fauzi Ichsan, an economist with Standard Chartered Bank in Jakarta.  \par \par \uc2 Still, some interbank players took profits against the rupiah, lifting the dollar from its intraday low of IDR9,430, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 "I think they took profits first as a precaution just in case other players were upset with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy too," a dealer with a local bank said.  \par \par \uc2 On the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the rupiah's rise, Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Tadjuddin didn't rule out such a move but said the bank leaves it to the market to determine the rupiah's "ideal value."  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said that the dollar-rupiah downtrend remains intact, but added that it will also depend on the outcome of U.S. trade data due Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers expect the dollar to trade between IDR9,400 and IDR9,500 Wednesday. The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will be closed Tuesday for a Muslim holiday.  \par \par \uc2 -By I Made Sentana, Dow Jones Newswires; 62 21 3983 1277; I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Hilary Mc Cully [ 09-01-06 1025GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1159 1848  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060109e219000ki\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
