\par\par \b \uc2 PRESS DIGEST-Indonesian Business News - Dec 13  \b0\par\par\uc2 368 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Dezember 2005\par 01:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 Following are the leading stories in the main Indonesian newspapers on Dec. 13. Reuters has not verified these stories and does not vouch for their accuracy. Telephone: Editorial: +62 21 384-6364. Fax: +62 21 344-8404 or Help Desk, +803 061 2124 (toll free).  \par \par \uc2 - - - -  \par \par \uc2 KOMPAS  \par \par \uc2 - \b \highlight22\uc2 INDONESIA\b0 \highlight\uc2  C.BANK GOV SAYS NO RUPIAH \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 There was no \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the recent strengthening of the rupiah \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <IDR=>, the bank's governor said on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 - - - -  \par \par \uc2 INVESTOR DAILY  \par \par \uc2 - INDONESIA KEEPS GUARANTEED DEPOSIT RATES UNCHANGED  \par \par \uc2 Indonesia's state-owned deposit insurance corporation (LPS) kept its maximum rupiah and dollar guaranteed deposit rates for Dec. 15 to Jan. 14 unchanged from the Nov. 15 to Dec. 14 period, LPS chief Krisna Wijaya said on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 - - - -  \par \par \uc2 BISNIS INDONESIA  \par \par \uc2 - \b \highlight22\uc2 CENTRAL BANK\b0 \highlight\uc2  ASKS FINANCE SECTOR TO MAKE SOME SACRIFICES  \par \par \uc2 Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  asked the country's banking sector to make some sacrifices for at least the next nine months as the economy was having tough times, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  would continue to implement a tight bias policy, the governor of Bank Indonesia said.  \par \par \uc2 - DAIHATSU INDONESIA SEES FLAT VEHICLE SALES IN 2006  \par \par \uc2 Daihatsu predicted full year sales of 50,000 units in the country next year, the same as its target for 2005, the distributor of the vehicle in Indonesia said.  \par \par \uc2 - MANDIRI SAYS READY TO FINANCE GRESIK'S NEW CEMENT PLANT  \par \par \uc2 Indonesia's largest lender, PT Bank Mandiri Tbk , said it is ready to finance the development of a new plant for the country's largest cement company, PT Semen Gresik Tbk , which could cost between 3.5-3.6 trillion rupiah, senior officials at those companies said.  \par \par \uc2 - CITRA MARGA PLANS 500 BLN RPH BOND ISSUE NEXT YEAR  \par \par \uc2 An Indonesian toll road operator, PT Citra Marga Nusaphala Persada Tbk , said it would like to raise 500 billion rupiah in bonds in the second half of 2006 to finance two toll road projects, a senior company official said.  \par \par \uc2 - - - -  \par \par \uc2 Looking for more information from local sources? For details, please call your local help desk <PHONE/HELP>  \par \par \uc2 PRESS-INDONESIA-BUSINESS|LANGEN|G|RBN|ABN|E|IF|REVU|RNP|DNP|PGE|PCO|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020051213e1cd0001a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
