\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  c.bank gov says no rupiah  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 176 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Dezember 2005\par 07:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds details)  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, Dec 12 (Reuters) - There was no \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the recent strengthening of the rupiah \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <IDR=>, the bank's governor said on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 When asked about the rupiah outlook, Burhanuddin Abdullah told reporters: "Let's see, the market will determine that."  \par \par \uc2 The rupiah gained more than 3 percent last week, which took its rise in the last 3 weeks to 5 percent, as foreigners poured money into Indonesian stocks and high-yielding bonds.  \par \par \uc2 An interest rate rise last week and expectations ta team of economic ministers sworn in last week would push for faster reforms and toughen the fight against Indonesia's mounting inflation boosted market sentiment.  \par \par \uc2 The rupiah, however, pared some of last week's sharp gains on Monday. It fell to about 9,730/9,740 per dollar at 0630 GMT, down from Friday's 5-1/2-month peak of 9,625.  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-INDONESIA-RUPIAH (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|IF|ABX|BNX|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020051212e1cc000b4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
