\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  Rupiah Ends Flat;Suspected Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 330 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 November 2005\par 10:29\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The Indonesian rupiah ended flat Tuesday as suspected Bank Indonesia dollar selling coupled with a hefty interest-rate hike helped the local unit recoupe its losses that were triggered earlier in the day by news of surging inflation in October, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar closed unchanged at IDR10,115.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said Bank Indonesia was suspected of selling dollars via state-banks when the greenback touched an intraday high of IDR10,200 earlier in the day, and again late in the late afternoon.  \par \par \uc2 "I strongly believe the state banks sold dollars on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a dealer with a foreign bank. "It was a disguised \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."  \par \par \uc2 The Central Statistics Agency reported Tuesday that the inflation rate surged to a higher-than expected 17.89% in October, following a fuel price hike on Oct. 1.  \par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia followed suit by raising its benchmark BI rate to 12.25%, its highest level since the middle of February 2003, from 11%.  \par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia may further hike the rate toward the end of the year to around 13%, said Paulus Nurwadono, the head of debt market research at Mandiri Securities.  \par \par \uc2 Rising interest rates in the short term will hurt sentiment toward local stocks and bonds, and could trigger rupiah-negative capital outflows, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The Jakarta Stock Exchange's main index ended down 0.12% Tuesday at 1064.953, reversing gains earlier in the day.  \par \par \uc2 Higher rates could also slow Indonesia's economic growth. Several analysts are ready to cut their 2005 growth forecast. Standard Chartered's Indonesian economist, Fauzi Ichsan, for one, said the bank will likely downgrade its forecast from 5.5%.  \par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will be closed Wednesday through Tuesday. The dollar may trade between IDR10,100 and IDR10,250 next week.  \par \par \uc2 -By I Made Sentana; Dow Jones Newswires; 62021 38831277; I-made.Sentana@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Paul Baylis [ 01-11-05 0929GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1159 1848  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020051101e1b1000cn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
