\par\par \b \uc2 Indonesia Rupiah Ends Steady; Capital Inflows To Bond Mkt  \b0\par\par\uc2 331 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 September 2005\par 12:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The Indonesian rupiah rebounded from an intraday low to close flat Thursday as capital inflows into the local bond market triggered wider dollar-selling, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar closed at IDR10,225, little-changed from its close Wednesday at IDR10,250. The greenback touched an intraday high of IDR10,700 earlier as the markets were disappointed with the government's rupiah-support program unveiled Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the program - which includes a planned reduction in fuel subsidy, reform on tax and investment regulations - lacks focus and doesn't set out a timetable for implementation.  \par \par \uc2 But the rupiah got a boost from London-based investors, who bought the government's rupiah bonds. Indonesian debt instruments took a beating recently due to rising interest rates and the rupiah's weakness.  \par \par \uc2 "We got some $20 million coming from these London-based investors," a dealer with a foreign bank said. "I think the total amount(including those received by other dealers)was around $100 million, not much, but enough to spark other players to sell the dollar."  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the they didn't detect any direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, but the nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might have sold dollars via state banks to help the rupiah.  \par \par \uc2 News that Indonesia had a higher-than expected trade surplus in July also spelt good news for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The official Central Statistics Agency reported Thursday that Indonesia's trade surplus widened to $2.17 billion from $2.01 billion in June. The average forecast of four analysts polled by Dow Jones Newswires was for a surplus of $1.87 billion.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers expect the dollar to trade between IDR10,150 and IDR10,600 Monday. The local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will be closed Friday due to a public holiday.  \par \par \uc2 -By I Made Sentana; Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277; I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com [ 01-09-05 1018GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1159 1848  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050901e191000l1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
