\par\par \b \uc2 Indonesia Rupiah Ends Higher On  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2 's Support  \b0\par\par\uc2 357 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 August 2005\par 11:51\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The Indonesian rupiah continued to recover Wednesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to help the beleaguered \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while the government was expected to announce complementary measures later in the day.  \par \par \uc2 Separately, Bank Indonesia chief Burhanuddin Abdullah said in Tokyo that the rupiah is undervalued by as much as 95%.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar closed at IDR10,200, lower than IDR10,525 Tuesday. The rupiah has now strengthened appreciably from IDR10,840 at the close Monday.  \par \par \uc2 To follow up a pledge made Tuesday, Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Wednesday, using short-term swap instruments and selling dollars in the spot market, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with swap instruments pushed the overnight premium earlier in the day to around 20% from 8% Tuesday, making it more expensive for market participants to maintain long dollar positions, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 "State banks, likely on behalf of Bank Indonesia, started to unload dollars in the spot market when the greenback was trading at IDR10,500," a dealer with a foreign bank said.  \par \par \uc2 Trading was calmer than Tuesday, with the market awaiting the government's measures to boost the rupiah.  \par \par \uc2 President Yudhoyono is expected to announce, among other things, a timetable for a further reduction of fuel subsidies, which have ballooned due to rising oil prices. Analysts have called on the government to reduce fuel subsidies to keep the state budget sustainable.  \par \par \uc2 Also Wednesday, Bank Indonesia senior deputy governor Miranda Gultom told Dow Jones Newswires that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will review regulations that may be impeding capital inflows into Indonesia. She declined to provide further details.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the country's benchmark stock index rose 1%, helped by the rupiah's recovery. The stock market's gains, if sustained, would help ease pressure on the rupiah as investors will need to buy the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to settle their purchases.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers expect the dollar to trade between IDR10,000 and IDR10,500 Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 -By I Made Sentana; Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277; I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Ven Ram [ 31-08-05 0951GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1159 1848  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050831e18v000ow\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
