\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar Rises Above IDR10,500 - Dealers  \b0\par\par\uc2 476 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 August 2005\par 07:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The U.S. dollar broke the IDR10,500 mark in intraday trade at 0455 GMT Monday for the first time since Jan. 2, 2002, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 "It (hit IDR10,500) in a very thin market when most dealers were away on lunch break," a dealer at a domestic commercial bank told Dow Jones Newswires.  \par \par \uc2 "The dollar was taken at IDR10,500 and is now being quoted around the 10,520 level."  \par \par \uc2 The greenback's latest record intraday high is likely to exacerbate market concerns about both the health of the rupiah and the severity of pending \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Indonesian government efforts to give the unit more traction against the greenback. [ 29-08-05 0511GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar has gained around 11% against the rupiah since January and was quoted as high as IDR10,475 Friday, its highest level since Jan. 2, 2002 before closing at IDR10,400. The close marked an acceleration from Thursday's IDR10,340.  \par \par \uc2 The greenback's surge has defied Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which have bled foreign reserves of more than $5 billion since April.  \par \par \uc2 On Friday, Bank Indonesia Governor Burhanuddin Abdullah vowed sterner policy measures to stem the rupiah's decline against the dollar including a new round of rate hikes. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier this month increased its benchmark Bank Indonesia rate to 8.75% from 8.50% to help support the rupiah.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week also began offering commercial banks the opportunity to park funds at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  overnight at a fixed 7% interest. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rolled out a new system earlier Monday allowing commercial banks to bid for rates of this overnight deposit facility that resulted in an average overnight deposit rate of 7.08%.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts have called for aggressive rate hikes above 10% and cuts in budget-crippling fuel price subsidies to decisively halt the rupiah's tumble against the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and government of President Susilo Bambang Yudhoyono must balance the potential boost those policies might provide the rupiah with wider negative impact. Rate hikes could threaten projected economic growth of 6.0% in 2005 and fuel-price increases could spark potentially destabilizing public protests.  \par \par \uc2 The Jakarta Stock Exchange composite index was down 3.6% at the close of midday trading Monday due to factors including negative market sentiment over the potential growth-curbing impact of additional pending interest rate increases.  \par \par \uc2 "A substantial rise in interest rates would likely torpedo (Indonesia's) economy (and) the decline in private consumption because of energy subsidy removal would likewise torpedo the economy," a Morgan Stanley research note issued Monday cautioned.  \par \par \uc2 -By I Made Sentana; Dow Jones Newswires; 62 21 3983 1277; I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Mary de Wet [ 29-08-05 0609GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050829e18t00070\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
