\par\par \b \uc2 Bank Indonesia Sells USD To Support Rupiah - Dealers  \b0\par\par\uc2 364 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 August 2005\par 05:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets Friday by selling dollars to try to boost a weakening rupiah, dealers told Dow Jones Newswires.  \par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia sold dollars to defend the rupiah at IDR10,370 at 0305 GMT, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 "Bank Indonesia is helping the rupiah somewhat (with dollar sales)," a dealer at a domestic commercial bank said. [ 26-08-05 0318GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is the latest in a series of dollar selling by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past week to slow the rupiah's decline. The dollar reached a new 43-month high of IDR10,425 midmorning Thursday. That compares with Wednesday's close of IDR10,340.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar eased to IDR10,408 at 0328 GMT Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 It may test IDR10,500 later on normal month-end corporate dollar purchases to fund overseas obligations, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia officials have said repeatedly in recent weeks that the bank will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets "if necessary" to defend the rupiah.  \par \par \uc2 Those \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have cost \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves of at least $5 billion since April and have been ineffective in reversing the rupiah's 8% on-year decline since January.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts have urged rupiah support policy measures, including aggressive interest rate hikes, cuts in fuel price subsidies and new foreign investment incentives to help increase \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflows.  \par \par \uc2 Coordinating Minister for the Economy Aburizal Bakrie said late Thursday that there will be a fuel price hike by end-2005. This hike follows the average 29% increase in March 1.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers and analysts say the government is likely reluctant to increase interest rates in the near future as the move might derail an economic growth target of 6.0% for 2005. Bank Indonesia earlier this month raised the benchmark rate to 8.75% from 8.50%.  \par \par \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  apparently prefers to continue foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  along with possible further measures, including tightening commercial banks' net open \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions and liquidity reductions by hiking rates of money market instruments, dealers said Friday.  \par \par \uc2 -By Jakarta Bureau; Dow Jones Newswires; 62 21 3983 1277; dj.jakarta@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Genevieve Soledad [ 26-08-05 0420GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050826e18q0003h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
