\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Rupiah drops, others weaker on stocks  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Vidya Ranganathan  \par \uc2 744 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 August 2005\par 05:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Aug 24 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah dropped nearly 2 percent on Wednesday to its weakest level in 3-\u189\'00\'BD years as foreigners selling Indonesian stocks and bonds added to pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  also fell as the Japanese yen <JPY=> retreated about a yen to the weaker side of 110 per dollar, oil prices rose back above $66 a barrel and regional equity markets stumbled.  \par \par \uc2 The rupiah <IDR=> extended a two-week-long slide to hit 10,300 per dollar, its lowest since February 2002 and marking one of its biggest single-day drops since May last year.  \par \par \uc2 Relentless demand for dollars to pay for oil imports, debt repayments and speculation drove the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down.  \par \par \uc2 Adding to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's woes, foreigners turned heavy sellers of Indonesian stocks <.JKSE> and bonds <0#IDBMK=> on Wednesday, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The rupiah is Asia's worst-performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year, having shed 5 percent this month and nearly 10 percent in 2005. The Jakarta stock index has fallen 14 percent this month.  \par \par \uc2 "It looks quite dicey. The BI has raised rates again but that does not seem to be helping the rupiah," said Thio Chin Loo, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with BNP Paribas.  \par \par \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BI) raised its 7-day \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate by a quarter point to 7.5 percent, but traders said interbank rates were much higher than the policy rate.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 , both verbally and by supplying dollars this month.  \par \par \uc2 It raised the benchmark rate on one-month paper by a quarter point on August 9 to 8.75 percent, and has been offering short-term deposits to absorb funds, making it more expensive to sell the rupiah short onshore.  \par \par \uc2 On Monday, Bank Indonesia scrapped a repurchase facility that allowed banks to borrow funds against bonds from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Analysts say policy is not tight enough to shore up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and demand for dollars to pay for oil is rising. Oil was above $66 a barrel <CLc1> on Wednesday, just below a record high above $67 hit earlier this month.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is structurally weak, partly from foreign debt repayments and partly from (oil) demand," said Craig Chan, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with Royal Bank of Scotland in Hong Kong.  \par \par \uc2 Low real interest rates were another factor, Chan said. With inflation running close to 8 percent and a benchmark one-month rate at 8.75 percent, analysts say there is little incentive for investors to hold Indonesian assets.  \par \par \uc2 BAHT WEAKER  \par \par \uc2 The Thai baht <THB=> fell nearly half a percent to the weaker side of 41 a dollar, the Singapore dollar <SGD=> and the Taiwan dollar <TWD=TP> also dropped nearly half a percent each.  \par \par \uc2 "We are seeing net foreign equity outflows, we are seeing equity indices coming off, dollar is on a bid tone and oil is remaining stubbornly high," Chan said.  \par \par \uc2 "So the demand for dollars from some of the oil importers is still there. In the near term, I continue to see a dollar-Asia bid."  \par \par \uc2 Chan said he expected the baht and the Taiwan dollar to be underperformers, partly because their trade accounts were deteriorating rapidly. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0818 GMT   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       110.63         109.84       -0.71\par  Sing dlr        1.6750         1.6676       -0.44\par  Taiwan dlr      32.275         32.125       -0.46\par  Korean won     1027.80        1027.30       -0.05\par  Baht             41.13          40.93       -0.49\par  Peso             56.05          55.96       -0.16\par  Rupiah        10280.00       10090.00       -1.85\par  Rupee            43.74          43.67       -0.15\par  Ringgit         3.7695         3.7690       -0.01\par  Yuan            8.1005         8.1012       +0.01\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       110.63         102.45       -7.39\par  Sing dlr        1.6750         1.6310       -2.63\par  Taiwan dlr      32.275         31.920       -1.10\par  Korean won     1027.80        1035.10       +0.71\par  Baht             41.13          38.88       -5.47\par  Peso             56.05          56.28       +0.41\par  Rupiah        10280.00        9290.00       -9.63\par  Rupee            43.74          43.47       -0.61\par  Ringgit         3.7695         3.8000       +0.81\par  Yuan            8.1005         8.2760       +2.17\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SI|Z|IF|PHD|J|SNS|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050824e18o000os\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgo