\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Indonesian rupiah at 3-1/2-year low of 10,225/dlr  \b0\par\par\uc2 399 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 August 2005\par 04:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates day's low, adds comment)  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Aug 24 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah extended its two-week-long slide to a fresh 3-1/2-year trough on Wednesday, driven by relentless demand for dollars for oil imports, debt repayments and speculation.  \par \par \uc2 The rupiah <IDR=> hit 10,225 per dollar, traders said, extending its decline this month to over 4 percent.  \par \par \uc2 "We are seeing a lot of onshore dollar demand and selling in the local stock and bond market," said one Jakarta-based trader.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said Bank Indonesia (BI) had been selling dollars through state-run banks to support the rupiah.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is structurally weak, partly from foreign debt repayments and partly from (oil) demand," said Craig Chan, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with Royal Bank of Scotland in Hong Kong.  \par \par \uc2 Low real interest rates were another factor, Chan said. With inflation running close to 8 percent and a benchmark one-month rate at 8.75 percent, analysts say there is little incentive for investors to hold Indonesian assets.  \par \par \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 , both verbally and by supplying dollars this month.  \par \par \uc2 It raised the benchmark rate on one-month paper by a quarter point on August 9 to 8.75 percent, and has been offering short-term deposits to absorb funds, making it more expensive to sell the rupiah short onshore.  \par \par \uc2 On Monday, Bank Indonesia scrapped a repurchase facility that allowed banks to borrow funds against bonds from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Analysts say policy is not tight enough to shore up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and the demand for dollars to pay for oil is rising. Oil was above $66 a barrel <CLc1> on Wednesday, just below a record high over $67 hit earlier this month.  \par \par \uc2 Nomura International downgraded Indonesian sovereign debt to sell from hold on Wednesday, citing high oil prices and possible new debt supply from the country.  \par \par \uc2 Chan, however, said offshore speculators and investors with limited access to Indonesian markets were turning cautious about selling the rupiah at these lofty levels.  \par \par \uc2 "It is a very risky \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to go into. Liquidity is tight. And if they took some measures you could be squeezed and lose all your profit or even make a loss," he said.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-RUPIAH (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|IF|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050824e18o000fk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
