\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Indonesia Rupiah Ends At 42-Month Low; Ignores Rate Hike  \b0\par\par\uc2 328 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 August 2005\par 14:04\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2005, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The Indonesian rupiah tumbled sharply to end at a 42-month low Wednesday as cyclical month-end dollar demand from local companies, combined with weak domestic capital markets, heightened the pressure on the local unit, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The market ignored a 25-basis point hike of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's one-week deposit rate as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was mainly driven by supply and demand, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The increase in Bank Indonesia's deposit rate wasn't followed by a rise in the weighted average rate of one-month Sertifikat Bank Indonesia, or SBI notes, which was unchanged at 8.75% during a weekly auction.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar closed at IDR10,280 compared with IDR10,095 Tuesday. This is the dollar's highest close since Feb. 6, 2002, when it ended at IDR10,315.  \par \par \uc2 The greenback briefly touched an intraday high of IDR10,320 but suspected Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pulled the unit below the IDR10,300 mark.  \par \par \uc2 Local companies and foreign investors bought dollars as there was no positive news for the rupiah, a dealer with a local bank said.  \par \par \uc2 Foreign investors continued selling Indonesian stocks and bonds Wednesday. The Jakarta Stock Exchange main index dropped 2.9% as foreign investors exited the local market following the rupiah's weakness.  \par \par \uc2 The yield of the government's rupiah five-year bonds rose to 14% from 13% Tuesday, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the dollar may revisit the IDR10,300 level Thursday due to continued month-end demand from local companies.  \par \par \uc2 'It's hard to predict the resistance level for the dollar with technical charts as the market is driven by genuine demand,' a dealer with a foreign bank said.  \par \par \uc2 Some dealers expect the dollar to rise to IDR10,400-IDR10,500 later this week.  \par \par \uc2 -By I Made Sentana, Dow Jones Newswires; 62 21 3983 1277; I-Made.Sentana&reg;dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Genevieve Soledad  \par \par \uc2 -0-  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020050824e18o008px\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
