\par\par \b \uc2 Indonesia Min: IDR Slide Against USD "Still Manageable"  \b0\par\par\uc2 396 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 August 2005\par 08:04\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The rupiah's continuing weakness against the U.S. dollar is "still manageable" in terms of its impact on the government's budgetary projections for this year, Minister of Finance Jusuf Anwar said Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar's rise Friday to break IDR10,000 won't hurt Indonesia's macroeconomic fundamentals, Anwar indicated to reporters.  \par \par \uc2 "The IDR10,000 mark is not a psychologically important level, it isn't sacred," he said. "Although there will be an impact on the budget, it's still manageable."  \par \par \uc2 Anwar didn't elaborate. [ 23-08-05 0625GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 The rupiah may yet strengthen against the greenback, and the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is healthy compared with other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Anwar said.  \par \par \uc2 His comments reflect government efforts to calm jittery markets as the dollar appears set to test IDR10,100 Tuesday after rising to a new 41-month high of IDR10,085 at the close of morning trade in the local market.  \par \par \uc2 The rupiah's fall defied suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market by Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which dealers said sold dollars around O300 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 Government officials and analysts are unanimous that the rupiah's weakness against the greenback is due to external factors, including record-high global crude-oil prices.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials have vowed to continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets "if necessary" to defend the rupiah.  \par \par \uc2 But analysts warn that such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bled \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves of more than $5 billion since April and has failed to reverse a more-than-5% tumble in the rupiah against the dollar since January.  \par \par \uc2 President Susilo Bambang Yudhoyono last week projected that the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves may fall to $27.1 billion by the end of next year from $32 billion now.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts say that Indonesia must take politically-risky policy measures, including raising interest rates and slashing budget-busting fuel-price subsidies to lend support to the rupiah.  \par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised the benchmark Bank Indonesia rate to 8.75% from 8.50%.  \par \par \uc2 Senior government officials have hinted that the government may increase fuel prices by early next year, having raised such rates by an average 29% on March 1.  \par \par \uc2 -By Farida Husna, Dow Jones Newswires; 62 21 3983 1277; dj.jakarta@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Ven Ram [ 23-08-05 0703GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050823e18n00077\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
