\par\par \b \uc2 Bank Indonesia Renews Dlr Sales To Defend IDR - Dealers   \b0\par\par\uc2 169 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 August 2005\par 06:26\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars for the second time Friday to stem the rupiah's slide, dealers said.   \par \par \uc2 "Bank Indonesia sold dollars again between IDR,9985 and IDR9,990," a dealer at a foreign bank in Jakarta said.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  follows Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar sales earlier Friday to stem the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slide against the dollar at the IDR9,980 mark. Those sales marked the third consecutive business day that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had acted to support the rupiah.   \par \par \uc2 The USD/IDR was at 9,985-95 at 0426 GMT.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is anxious to prevent the dollar from rising above what dealers call a crucial "psychological threshold" of IDR10,000.   \par \par \uc2 The IDR10,000 mark may spur jittery investors to dump the rupiah, which could further weigh on the unit.   \par \par \uc2 -By Jakarta Bureau, Dow Jones Newswires, 62 21 3983 1277; dj.jakarta@dowjones.com   \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Lena Lee [ 19-08-05 0439GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050819e18j00038\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
