\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Weaker as equity sell-off bites  \b0\par\par\uc2 763 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 August 2005\par 05:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Aug 19 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were knocked down against the dollar on Friday by a sell-off in stocks, with the Taiwan dollar at a seven-month trough and Indonesia's rupiah hitting a 3-\u189\'00\'BD year low near the pivotal 10,000 per dollar level.  \par \par \uc2 Equity markets weakened partly on persistent worries that high oil prices are squeezing company profits and consumer spending. This set the tone for regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The Taiwan dollar <TWD=TP> eased about a quarter of a percent from Thursday's close to 32.19 per U.S. dollar, its weakest level since mid-January.  \par \par \uc2 The South Korean won <KRW=><KRW=KTFC> eased as much as 0.7 percent to 1,025.8 per dollar, its lowest level in nearly three weeks, while the Singapore dollar <SGD=D4> fell more than half a percent to a three-week trough at 1.6710 per U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "The U.S. dollar should go up slowly because stock markets in Asia are not doing so well," said a Singapore-based trader.  \par \par \uc2 "The market has been short of dollars in the last couple of weeks, so there is a covering of positions."  \par \par \uc2 Foreign funds have been net sellers of Taiwan stocks all week. They sold a net 6.127 billion Taiwan dollars on Friday -- the heaviest selling so far this month. In South Korea, foreign investors continued to offload local stocks, taking their total net sales this week to around 334 billion won.  \par \par \uc2 AILING RUPIAH  \par \par \uc2 The rupiah <IDR=> touched a low of about 9,995 per dollar but recovered slightly after traders suspected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the ailing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday it will continue dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the rupiah, which has shed almost seven percent against the dollar this year.  \par \par \uc2 Costly oil, which state oil firm Pertamina has been forced to import in increasing amounts to meet a domestic shortfall, and outflows of capital have been key reasons for the rupiah's slide.  \par \par \uc2 The latest sell-off comes as traders target the psychological 10,000 rupiah per dollar level, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to hold onto important chart support in the 9,900 area earlier this week.  \par \par \uc2 "Until the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  responds more vigorously with monetary policy, it will struggle to achieve its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  objectives," said HSBC \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Richard Yetsenga.  \par \par \uc2 The interest rate on one-month \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  certificates <BISBI01> has risen by more than 130 basis points this year. Still, real interest rates are barely positive after taking into account annual inflation running close to 8 percent.  \par \par \uc2 The Philippine peso <PHP=> weakened about a fifth of a percent to a 1-\u189\'00\'BD week low of 56.05 per dollar, but pulled away from that level thanks to commercial demand for pesos and technical support, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said optimism the Philippine Supreme Court would lift a freeze on a key sales tax, perhaps as soon as next week, prevented a bigger peso sell-off this week. The sales tax is the centrepiece of the government's economic reforms.  \par \par \uc2 The peso has shed about 0.7 percent against the dollar this week, while the rupiah has lost almost 2 percent and the Singapore and South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have eased about 1 percent each.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day at   0818 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       110.74         110.10       -0.58\par  Sing dlr        1.6685         1.6609       -0.46\par  Taiwan dlr      32.186         32.114       -0.22\par  Korean won     1025.50        1018.70       -0.66\par  Baht             41.30          41.20       -0.24\par  Peso             56.02          55.93       -0.16\par  Rupiah         9985.00        9940.00       -0.45\par  Rupee            43.59          43.56       -0.06\par  Ringgit         3.7650         3.7680       +0.08\par  Yuan            8.1047         8.1007       -0.05\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       110.74         102.45       -7.49\par  Sing dlr        1.6685         1.6310       -2.25\par  Taiwan dlr      32.186         31.920       -0.83\par  Korean won     1025.50        1035.10       +0.94\par  Baht             41.30          38.88       -5.86\par  Peso             56.02          56.28       +0.46\par  Rupiah         9985.00        9290.00       -6.96\par  Rupee            43.59          43.47       -0.26\par  Ringgit         3.7650         3.8000       +0.93\par  Yuan            8.1047         8.2760       +2.11\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SI|Z|IF|PHD|J|SNS|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050819e18j000ws\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100