\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Bank  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  to keep  \highlight22\uc2 intervening \highlight\uc2 , govt has doubts   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Harry Suhartono and Adriana Nina Kusuma   \par \uc2 512 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 August 2005\par 06:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, Aug 19 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday it will continue dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the ailing rupiah, even after the chief economic minister said it was not effective and called for fuel subsidy cuts instead.   \par \par \uc2 Pressured by rising oil costs, the rupiah <IDR=> has fallen almost 7 percent against the dollar this year, and on Friday it hit a 3-\u189\'00\'BD year low near the pivotal 10,000 per dollar level.   \par \par \uc2 "I saw that the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still effective. There is no strong macro and fundamental reason for the rupiah to get weaker," Aslim Tadjuddin, a deputy governor of Bank Indonesia, told Reuters.   \par \par \uc2 "We are in the market. We always monitor the fluctuations in exchange rates and we are going to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if necessary," Tadjuddin said in a telephone interview.   \par \par \uc2 But Aburizal Bakrie, the government's chief economic minister, said earlier that it would be better in the long run if hefty domestic fuel subsidies were cut.   \par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is only a temporary thing. The question is whether we should do all that? I think it is more important to reduce the subsidy," Bakrie told reporters.   \par \par \uc2 "With such huge fuel subsides, the rupiah will weaken. The situation is that we need to keep on supporting subsidies so we need to keep on buying dollars. If we keep on purchasing dollars, the dollar will become stronger," he added.   \par \par \uc2 The fuel subsidy and Indonesia's import system entail oil and energy product purchases that must be made in dollars by the state oil company, and which add to the government's already massive debt.   \par \par \uc2 OIL WOES   \par \par \uc2 Despite its membership of the Organisation of Petroleum Exporting Countries, Indonesia has become a net crude importer due to various problems causing a decline in production.   \par \par \uc2 President Susilo Bambang Yudhoyono has warned that should world oil prices remain around current levels, fuel subsidies for 2005 could cost more than 140 trillion rupiah ($14.2 billion), nearly double the stated amount in the budget.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts and traders have said dollar buying of up to $1 billion each month by state oil company Pertamina to finance oil imports is putting a significant burden on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The government and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  have put in place several measures to defend the rupiah, including restricting Pertamina's dollar buying to appointed state banks.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also raised benchmark interest rates in to contain rising inflation and help the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The interest rate on one-month \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  certificates (SBI) <BISBI01> has risen by more than 130 basis points this year.   \par \par \uc2 At the last auction, the one-month SBI certificate yielded 8.75 percent, to be in line with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's newly introduced reference interest rate.   \par \par \uc2 Some analysts say Indonesia needs to raise interest rates further and keep lowering domestic oil subsidies to halt the slide in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   