\par\par \b \uc2 Indonesian rupiah needs rate rise support-analysts   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Vidya Ranganathan   \par \uc2 616 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 August 2005\par 06:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Aug 19 (Reuters) - Indonesia needs to raise interest rates further and keep lowering domestic oil subsidies to halt the slide in the rupiah, as its dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not achieving results, analysts said on Friday.   \par \par \uc2 The rupiah <IDR=> weakened to a 3-\u189\'00\'BD year low of 9,995 a dollar on Friday, close to the pivotal 10,000-per-dollar level. Losses in the past week have exceeded 2 percent, even after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent some of its foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves trying to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily this week. After confirming the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday, Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman Halim Alamsyah said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was open to other options to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 "That's a sign that the ammunition is running low without really producing the desired effect," said Tim Condon, head of research at ING in Singapore.   \par \par \uc2 "They fundamentally have a wrong policy mix, a rupiah-unfriendly policy mix," he said.   \par \par \uc2 The country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves stood at $32.5 billion on August 5 -- covering about 7 months of imports -- after it had spent $5 billion in 3 months supporting emerging Asia's worst performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year.   \par \par \uc2 The mounting cost of oil, which state oil firm Pertamina has been forced to import in increasing amounts to meet a domestic shortfall, and outflows of capital have been primary reasons for the rupiah's slide.   \par \par \uc2 In early July, Bank Indonesia said Pertamina would get dollars to pay for its oil imports from the government's account with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , hoping to ease pressure on the rupiah, but the oil firm has since been spotted buying dollars in the market.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts said Indonesia could cut subsidies on domestic fuel further, thereby encouraging consumers to become more efficient users of expensive oil and easing pressure on the budget. Indonesia's chief economic minister Aburizal Bakrie said on Friday the effectiveness of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was temporary and it was more important to reduce the subsidies.   \par \par \uc2 RATES   \par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia adopted a more transparent inflation-targeting policy last month, changing its main policy tool to the rate on its one-month paper <ID1MSBI=BIIA>. It even surprised markets by raising that rate by a quarter point to 8.75 percent on August 9.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  needs to do a lot more of policy tightening if it wants to conserve its dwindling reserves, with real interest rates barely positive after taking into account annual inflation running close to 8 percent.   \par \par \uc2 "Their option is really to switch to rate tightening and they are increasingly moving in that direction," said Claudio Piron, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with JPMorgan Chase.   \par \par \uc2 Indonesia tended to have a relatively higher pass-through of a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  into inflation, and hence it was imperative Bank Indonesia prevent the rupiah from falling too much, he said.   \par \par \uc2 In June the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  imposed restrictions on foreigners' holdings of rupiah onshore and access to hedging instruments.   \par \par \uc2 "The underlying situation is that there is heavy dollar demand and trying to deal with that through \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls will not help," he said, referring to the possibility of other restrictions being imposed on rupiah trade.   \par \par \uc2 Piron said the relationship between rising oil prices and the depletion in Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves was strengthening, and every dollar rise in the Dubai crude <DUB-1M-A> corresponded to an almost $300 million fall in reserves.   \par \par \uc2 "The cost-benefit analysis will increasingly come down to whether it would be more beneficial to raise interest rates instead," Piron said in a note.   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-RUPIAH-\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|M|D|O|OIL|IF|DNP|PEN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050819e18j0008q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
