\par\par \b \uc2 Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  Dep: To  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  In  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Mkt "If Necessary"   \b0\par\par\uc2 452 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 August 2005\par 04:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market "if necessary", but it has no plan to introduce new regulations to defend the rupiah, Aslim Tadjudin, a deputy governor at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 "We are monitoring the rupiah and there is no doubt that we are trying to defend the rupiah," Aslim told Dow Jones Newswires in a telephone interview.   \par \par \uc2 The rupiah fell to a fresh 41-month low of IDR9,935 to the U.S. dollar at 0212 GMT Thursday versus its previous close of IDR9,920 as high oil prices continued to hurt sentiment. Capital outflows from the local stock market, and dollar purchases by companies to hedge their offshore debts, also weighed. [ 18-08-05 0224GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 Aslim declined to say if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had already sold dollars Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 "We have done a lot" in efforts to defend the rupiah, he said when asked if Bank Indonesia had any plan to introduce new regulations in the near future to help the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 He referred to regulations which Bank Indonesia introduced in June to limit dollar-rupiah transactions by foreigners; the steps also limited PT Pertamina's dollar purchases in the market, and asked state companies to repatriate their export revenues.   \par \par \uc2 In addition, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in late July raised the one-month dollar deposit rate that the government guarantees for August to 3% from 2.75% to discourage people from moving their dollars out of Indonesia.   \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will monitor the development of the Jakarta Interbank Offered Dollar Rate to decide whether it will raise the guarantee rate or not at the end of the month," Aslim said.   \par \par \uc2 He added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would also request banks in Jakarta to stop asking depositors to change their dollars into rupiah when they wanted to deposit dollars locally. Banks usually convert depositors' dollars into rupiah at less favorable exchange rates in such cases.   \par \par \uc2 "Banks here should stop doing that if they want to attract customers," Aslim said. He added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, would not issue a ruling on the matter as "it's a matter of business strategy."   \par \par \uc2 Aslim repeated that the main culprits for the rupiah's weakness were "external factors" such as high oil prices and the dollar's rise against the yen early Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 Some dealers said it was only a matter of time before the dollar reached IDR10,000.   \par \par \uc2 Aslim said he hoped the dollar wouldn't rise to that psychologically important level.   \par \par \uc2 -By I Made Sentana; Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277; I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com   \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Andrew Torchia [ 18-08-05 0319GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050818e18i0001x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
