\par\par \b \uc2 =DJ  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  ASIA:Reserves Not Enough To Support Indonesian Rupiah   \b0\par\par\uc2 1,215 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 August 2005\par 17:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2005, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 By Phelim Kyne and I Made Sentana   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par      A Dow Jones Newswires Column\par   JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--Indonesia should aggressively raise interest rates and remove obstacles to inward flows of capital to avert a hemorrhage in the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign- exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves, which have been deployed to support a weakening rupiah, analysts say.\par   The prediction follows \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for a second business day in a row Thursday to support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which fell to a fresh 41-month (low against the U.S. dollar.\par   Bank Indonesia sold dollars at IDR9,975, according to market participants to stop the greenback from surging above what dealers say is a key 'psychological threshold' of IDR10,000.\par   The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gave the rupiah some traction. The dollar closed at IDR9,950, down from both an intraday high of IDR9,975 and Tuesday's close of IDR9,920\par   But \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has so far cost the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at least $5 billion since April and has failed to trim a more than 5% slide in the rupiah against the U.S. dollar since the beginning of the year.\par   Some say the rupiah purchases aren't sustainable and a broader course of action is need to support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par   Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  poses a serious threat to the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves, said Irene Cheung, ABN Amro Bank's regional head of sovereign and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategy.\par   Despite the expense of supporting the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Bank Indonesia Deputy Governor Aslim Tadjudin told Dow Jones Newswires that he hoped the dollar wouldn't hit the IDR10,000 mark and that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will continue to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  'if necessary' to defend the unit. He didn't elaborate further.\par   Indonesia's 2006 budget, unveiled Monday, forecast an erosion in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves to $27.1 billion by the end of next year from $37.4 billion in March. Currently, the reserves stand at $32.5 billion.\par   'It appears that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has resolved to cap the USD/IDR at below the 10,000 mark...(so) in our view the economy runs the risk of still slower growth and sharply lower foreign reserves,' ABN AMRO's Cheung said in a research note.\par   Cheung expects that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will raise interest rates to support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and forecasts that the one-month Sertifikat Bank Indonesia rate or the benchmark Bank Indonesia rate will rise to as high as 9.75% in the next six months to bolster the rupiah.\par   The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last week hiked the Bank Indonesia rate to 8.75% from 8.50%.\par   Record-high global oil prices are in part to blame for the rupiah's fall and are playing havoc with Indonesia's macroeconomic stability. September Nymex global crude oil prices were up 35 cents to $63.60 at 0924 GMT Thursday.\par    USD/IDR10,000 Imminent Without Policy Initiatives\par   Surging oil prices have fueled an acceleration in Indonesia's inflation to 7.84% on-year in July from 7.42% in June, which has weighed on the rupiah and slowed economic growth in the second quarter to 5.54% on-year from 6.19% on-year in the first three months of 2005.\par   The rupiah has also suffered as the U.S. dollar has strengthened against major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cross Asia.\par   'Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reduced the dollar's gains, but its upward trend remains intact,' a dealer with a domestic commercial bank said.\par   The dollar is likely to break the IDR10,000 mark by early September unless there is urgent monetary and macroeconomic policy moves to stem the rupiah's slide, said Standard Chartered economist Fauzi Ichsan.\par   'The government and Bank Indonesia need to do the right thing by introducing the right policy package including hiking interest rates....to more than 10% to make it meaningful.' Ichsan said.\par   The government also needs to open Indonesia's choked inflows of dollars by reviving an official state firm privatization program, he said. The government should also fast-track other initiatives to increase investment injections into the economy, he added.\par   Indonesia's official 2005 budget calls for revenue of IDR3.5 trillion from stake share sales this year, but analysts say the government has effectively sidelined the program.\par   If those policies are put in place, the dollar could fall to IDR9,500 by the end of next year, slightly higher than an official budget projection of an average IDR9,400 for all of 2006, Ichsan said.\par   The measures should include rigorous enforcement of a government regulation that requires exporters to repatriate \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  earnings, said Bank Mandiri's (BMRI.JK) chief economist, Martin Panggabean\par   But enforcing compliance with that rule will be difficult, ABN Amro's Cheung suggested, and require sterner policy measures.\par   'In this environment of a falling rupiah, exporters would even be more tempted to keep their dollar receipts overseas,' she said.\par      Regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Swap Deals Unlikely To Help\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cheung instead urged a follow-up to a March 1 average 29% hike in fuel prices and an 'appropriate adjustment' in the rupiah's value to protect the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves. Cheung didn't elaborate on what the 'appropriate' level should be. Failure to avert a decline in the rupiah to IDR10,000 against the greenback would create a dangerous 'domino effect' of accelerating inflation and ever-higher interest rates that would choke economic growth, said Juniman a senior economist at Bank Internasional Indonesia (BNII.JK). He, like many Indonesians, has only one name, 'It's an important psychological mark because when (the dollar/rupiah rate) hits 10,000, you can expect marked shrinkage in volume because the supply of dollars will dry up...(but) pressure on the rupiah will remain,' Standard Chartered's Ichsan said. Indonesia is also unlikely to gain any assistance from \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -swap agreements between Association of Southeast Asian Nation members and Japan, China and South Korea. The group, known as Asean+3, in May agreed to increase the size of the program, under the Chiang Mai Initiative, which was set up following the 1997-98 Asian financial crisis to help cash-strapped countries defend their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in times of crisis. But Indonesia lacks the requisite International Monetary Fund program or equivalent that potential recipients of the Initiative require, Ichsan said. Indonesia last year ended participation in an IMF economic bailout program begun after the financial crisis. Still, the rupiah may yet strengthen as external factors that have so heavily weighted on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in recent months weaken, said BNP Paribas senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analyst Thio Chin Loo. 'Oil prices have slowed quite sharply overnight and if that continues, it should alleviate some the pressure on the rupiah,' Thio said. 'If oil prices decline, the only remaining risk is a rising dollar, which could cause the rupiah to test IDR10,000 (against the dollar).' -By Phelim Kyne and I Made Sentana, Dow Jones Newswires; 62 21 3983 1277; phelim.kyne@dowjones.com (Phelim Kyne has reported from Taiwan, Cambodia and China and is currently Dow Jones Newswires' bureau Chief for Indonesia; I Made Sentana is a ten-year veteran of Indonesian economic and financial news reporting and senior correspondent in Dow Jones Newswires' Jakarta bureau) -Edited by Iain McDonald - -    \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020050818e18i00a9h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
