\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Mostly steady, rupiah hits 3-\u189\'00\'BD year low   \b0\par\par\uc2 718 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 August 2005\par 04:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Aug 18 (Reuters) - Indonesia's rupiah hit a fresh 3-\u189\'00\'BD year low on Thursday but recovered slightly after \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were little moved against the dollar.   \par \par \uc2 A retreat in oil prices, which hit a record high of $67.10 last Friday, supported regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , hurt this week by worries that firm oil prices would dent economic growth.   \par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar <SGD=> <SGD=D4> and South Korean won <KRW=> <KRW=KTFC> pulled away from two-week lows hit against the dollar on Wednesday. The Thai baht <THB=> was up about a fifth of a percent at 41.19 per dollar -- above Wednesday's almost two-week trough at 41.33.   \par \par \uc2 The rupiah <IDR=> hogged the spotlight as it stepped closer to the key psychological level of 10,000 rupiah per dollar.   \par \par \uc2 Domestic demand for dollars pushed the rupiah to a 3-\u189\'00\'BD year low of about 9,980, before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to support the battered \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 A Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman confirmed the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Seeking to support the rupiah, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also said it would offer four-day instruments carrying an interest rate of 5.75 percent on Thursday to absorb excess rupiah liquidity.   \par \par \uc2 "Everyone is focusing on the 10,000 level, whether or not it goes and when," said Callum Henderson, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at Standard Chartered Bank in Singapore.   \par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be an obstacle to this in the short term. But more weakness is likely -- you have a balance of payments deterioration because Indonesia is a net oil importer, capital inflows are not picking up the slack, while interest rates are too low," Henderson said.   \par \par \uc2 The rupiah has lost more than 6 percent of its value since the start of the year, due mainly to rising inflation and soaring oil prices, which have increased dollar buying to finance oil imports. It has shed about 1.5 percent this week.   \par \par \uc2 RINGGIT WEAKER   \par \par \uc2 Malaysia's ringgit <MYR=> dipped to its weakest level since the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unpegged from the dollar a month ago, pressured by foreign investors selling local assets, traders said.   \par \par \uc2 They said the ringgit eased to a low of 3.7695 per dollar, taking it to its weakest level since July 22 -- the day after Malaysia abandoned the ringgit's peg to the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 "Initially, when investors bought the ringgit at 3.8 they parked the money in ringgit assets, in bonds and equities," said one dealer in Kuala Lumpur.   \par \par \uc2 "When the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tested the 3.7450 area it looked quite strong but didn't move further, so most investors sold their bonds and converted their ringgit back into dollars."   \par \par \uc2 Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were also likely to be held back by equity flows into Japan from the rest of Asia, dealers said.   \par \par \uc2 Foreign investors bought a net 721.9 billion yen ($6.58 billion) of Japanese stocks last week, up from 495 billion yen the previous week, official data from Japan showed on Thursday. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day at   0815 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       110.10         109.85       -0.23\par  Sing dlr        1.6609         1.6615       +0.04\par  Taiwan dlr      32.111         32.066       -0.14\par  Korean won     1018.50        1018.00       -0.05\par  Baht             41.20          41.27       +0.17\par  Peso             55.93          55.90       -0.04\par  Rupiah         9940.00        9900.00       -0.40\par  Rupee            43.55          43.54       -0.03\par  Ringgit         3.7680         3.7650       -0.08\par  Yuan            8.1007         8.0997       -0.01\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       110.10         102.45       -6.95\par  Sing dlr        1.6609         1.6310       -1.80\par  Taiwan dlr      32.111         31.920       -0.59\par  Korean won     1018.50        1035.10       +1.63\par  Baht             41.20          38.88       -5.63\par  Peso             55.93          56.28       +0.63\par  Rupiah         9940.00        9290.00       -6.54\par  Rupee            43.55          43.47       -0.18\par  Ringgit         3.7680         3.8000       +0.85\par  Yuan            8.1007         8.2760       +2.16\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SI|Z|IF|PHD|J|SNS|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050818e18i000nk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
