\par\par \b \uc2 Indonesian rupiah slips to 3-\u189\'00\'BD year low vs dlr   \b0\par\par\uc2 241 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 August 2005\par 03:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Aug 18 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah weakened to its lowest level since March 2002 against the dollar on Thursday, extending this week's losses on domestic demand for dollars.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers said while the move in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unusual given a pull-back in high oil prices, which has battered the rupiah, sentiment towards the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained weak.   \par \par \uc2 The rupiah was catching up with weakness in other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the previous session, when Indonesian markets were closed for a holiday, they said.   \par \par \uc2 The rupiah shed about a third of a percent from late Asian trading levels on Tuesday to 9,935 per dollar <IDR=> by 0155 GMT, its weakest level in about 3-\u189\'00\'BD years.   \par \par \uc2 "Oil prices are sliding but there is still corporate demand for dollars," said one Jakarta-based trader.   \par \par \uc2 He said market wariness of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the rupiah could limit \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  losses, but that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had not been sighted so far on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped the rupiah move off its lows.   \par \par \uc2 The rupiah has lost more than six percent of its value since the start of the year, due mainly to rising inflation and soaring oil prices, which have increased the dollar buying of state oil company Pertamina to finance oil imports.   \par \par \uc2 