\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Indonesia Rupiah Ends At 41-Mo Low On High Oil Prices   \b0\par\par\uc2 322 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 August 2005\par 12:19\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2005, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The Indonesian rupiah closed at a 41-month low against the dollar Tuesday as high oil prices and capital outflows from the local stock market hurt the local unit, dealers said.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar closed at IDR9,920 versus Monday's close of IDR9,885. This was the greenback's highest close since March 19, 2002 when it closed at IDR9,980.   \par \par \uc2 It touched an intraday high of IDR9,925 earlier in the day, but suspected Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  capped the dollar's rise, dealers said.   \par \par \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Burhanuddin Abdullah said Tuesday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is always ready to help the rupiah, which is being hit by 'external factors' such as rising oil prices in the global market and rising U.S. rates. Abdullah, however, didn't mention whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had sold dollars Tuesday as dealers suspected.   \par \par \uc2 'Rising oil prices still roiled sentiment on the rupiah,' a dealer with a foreign bank said.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers said capital outflows from the Indonesian stock market also contributed to the rupiah's slide. The Jakarta Stock Exchange's main index fell 0.4% to a five-week low after a 3% drop Monday.   \par \par \uc2 Elsewhere in the money market, the weighted average rate of Bank Indonesia's on-month SBI notes rose to 8.75% in a weekly auction Tuesday from 8.71%. The SBI rate is now at the same level as the benchmark BI rate.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is under pressure to raise the benchmark rate again, likely next month, to help the rupiah and to cool inflation.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers expect the dollar to trade between IDR9,810 and IDR9,950 Thursday. The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will be closed Wednesday for Indonesia's Independence Day. -By I Made Sentana, Dow Jones Newswires; 62 21 3983 1277; I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com   \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Paul Baylis   \par \par \uc2 -0-   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020050816e18g005se\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
