\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 CENTRAL BANK \highlight\uc2  WATCH: Indonesia Rupiah Defense Ops Failing  \b0\par\par\uc2 991 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 August 2005\par 09:39\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par      By Phelim Kyne \par      A Dow Jones Newswires Column \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  campaign to stem a slide in the value of the rupiah to help fight inflationary pressures hasn't worked and is unsustainable, analysts say.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should instead further tighten monetary policy to beat inflation and support the rupiah, they say.  \par \par \uc2 Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has lost 5% of its value since the start of the year despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  running down its foreign reserves by $5 billion to defend the unit.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has put on a brave face, saying that it has stabilized the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "We are quite confident that our actions have stabilized (the rupiah)," Bank Indonesia's economic research and monetary policy directorate head, Perry Warjiyo, said Friday.  \par \par \uc2 But the slide in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has delivered a black eye to the government of President Susilo Bambang Yudhoyono by both skewering sunny official USD/IDR projections and fueling a hemorrhage in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.  \par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia Senior Deputy Governor Miranda Gultom said last month that the official USD/IDR target of an average of 9,300 for 2005 was unfeasible.  \par \par \uc2 Official pessimism about the rupiah deepened last week when Coordinating Minister for the Economy, Aburizal Bakrie, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  probably wouldn't rally against the dollar in the second half of 2005 and a USD/IDR average of 9,750 was likely in the same time period.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar was trading at IDR9,793 at 0445 GMT Tuesday, below a more-than-three-year high of IDR9,870 set on July 5 but well above IDR9,290 at the start of 2005.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has spent nearly USD5 billion - or 14% of its \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves - and increased interest rates by 110bps since April 2005 to support the rupiah," UBS said in a recent note. "Yet, the IDR has continued to weaken (and) though \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves at $32 billion currently are still adequate, \b \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  of such a scale are obviously not sustainable over the medium-term."  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par      Interest Rate Hikes Advised \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia has gradually raised its benchmark rate to 8.5% from a record low of 7.32% in May 2004 in response to rising inflationary momentum.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But some say the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  needs to be more aggressive.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 UBS predicts the rupiah will further slide to IDR10,000 against the dollar by the end of this year and hit IDR10,600 by the end of 2006 without more aggressive monetary tightening policies in the short term.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The International Monetary Fund, which guided Indonesia's recovery from the 1997-98 Asian financial crisis, last month also suggested interest rate hikes to contain inflation.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But such measures are unlikely in the short-to-medium term due to Bank Indonesia's monetary policy direction drift, said JP Morgan Chase economist Sin Ben Ong.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We tend to think that the rupiah (weakness) is symptomatic of a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that's too lax in running monetary policy," Ong said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Rather than risk the political fallout of raising interest rates to dampen the "mild overheating" in the Indonesian economy, Bank Indonesia is opting to address inflationary pressure through \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Ong said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is constrained by political considerations to raise interest rates...so it has \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets," he said. "Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is concerned about (the rupiah's decline) because it has an immediate knock on effect on inflation in two-three months that lasts four to five months."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia is candid about the difficult monetary policy balancing act it's pursuing  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "What we are facing now is the dilemma of boosting macro-economic growth and maintaining macro-economic stability," Bank Indonesia's Warjiyo said last week.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    Rupiah Strengthening Requires Investment Surge \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 There's political wisdom in addressing inflation through \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates. The alternative, aggressively raising interest rates, could sabotage an official economic target of 6% on-year growth for 2005.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Inflationary pressure also increases the threat of noisy public protests about rising prices and potential social instability that dogged Yudhoyono's predecessor, Megawati Sukarnoputri.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A 29% average hike in fuel prices in March prompted a surge in inflation to 8.12% year-on-year in April. Inflation has since eased to 7.84% on-year in July, but outpaces an upwardly revised inflation target of 7.5% for full-year 2005.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 While the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  monetary policy juggles social and political stability concerns with macroeconomic realities, analysts suggest that only an injection of desperately-needed foreign investment will give the rupiah decisive traction against the greenback.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia's economy needs investment dollars to correct an "imbalance in the system" that is weighing on the rupiah, said Irene Cheung, ABN Amro Bank's regional head of sovereign and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategy. "I don't see in the near term any positive for the rupiah...(and) I'm concerned about the rupiah until (foreign investment) money starts coming into the country."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Pallid investor sentiment fueled a 26% on-year decline in approved foreign direct investment to $10.3 billion in 2004.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But Indonesia's official Investment Coordinating Board said last month that the country recorded a 70% on-year rise in actual FDI to $3.35 billion in the first six months of 2005. Indonesia's pledged FDI surged 71% to $5.93 billion in the same period.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 That data supports UBS' projection that FDI will provide needed support for the rupiah in the months ahead.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We remain confident that Indonesia will be able to attract FDI inflows and that residents will repatriate capital over the medium-term, thus providing support to the IDR," the UBS research note said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Phelim Kyne; Dow Jones Newswires; 62 21 3983 1277; phelim.kyne@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Phelim Kyne has reported from Taiwan, Cambodia and China and is currently Dow Jones Newswires' bureau chief for Indonesia)  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Iain McDonald [ 09-08-05 0739GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1186 4253  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050809e189000eu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
