\par\par \b \uc2 Bk Indonesia: Has Stabilised Rupiah Exchange Rate  \b0\par\par\uc2 174 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 August 2005\par 11:36\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign-exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has likely stabilized the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's exchange rate against the U.S. dollar, a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said Friday.  \par \par \uc2 "We are quite confident that our actions have stabilized" the rupiah, said Perry Warjiyo, head of the economic research and monetary policy directorate at Bank Indonesia.  \par \par \uc2 He said the government's moves to impose capital controls are also likely supporting the rupiah.  \par \par \uc2 "Of course, we see blips" in the exchange rate, Warjiyo said at an economics forum in Singapore.  \par \par \uc2 The rupiah is down around 4% versus the U.S. dollar from the start of the year, but has gained gradually in recent weeks after reaching its weakest point this year on July 5.  \par \par \uc2 UBS estimates that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  since April cost the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  almost $5 billion, or 14% of its total reserves.  \par \par \uc2 -By Oliver Biggadike, Dow Jones Newswires; +65-6415-4044; oliver.biggadike@dowjones.com.  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by E. Beiser [ 05-08-05 0953GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050805e185000ep\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
