\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Indonesia key rate stays at 8.49 pct for third week  \b0\par\par\uc2 380 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juli 2005\par 03:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds details, comments)  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, July 27 (Reuters) - Indonesia kept key one-month interest rates unchanged at 8.49 percent for the third week in a row in an auction on Wednesday, just shy of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recently introduced 8.50 percent target.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the result was a sign of Bank Indonesia's desire to underline the importance of the new policy target by keeping rates as close as possible to it.  \par \par \uc2 The market had forecast one-month \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  paper, or SBIs, would rise one basis point to match the target, known as the reference rate.  \par \par \uc2 "I think it sent a strong message to the market that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wants the SBI rate to hover at around the reference rate despite the weak rupiah," a dealer at a large local bank said.  \par \par \uc2 "They can use other tools to strengthen the rupiah such as through \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."  \par \par \uc2 Authorities steer SBIs, \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's benchmark short-term debt, through weekly auctions.  \par \par \uc2 The country introduced a target for one-month SBIs in early July in a move to make monetary policy more transparent and increase confidence in the rupiah.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  took 38 trillion rupiah from the auction, against 39.4 trillion maturing Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said that suggested short-term rates, including overnight rates, may remain low due to the expected ample liquidity in the banking system.  \par \par \uc2 The rupiah was quoted at around 9,814/34 per dollar on Wednesday, weaker than 9,808 on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has lost more than five percent against the dollar this year and is the third-worst performing Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  behind the Japanese yen and Thai baht.  \par \par \uc2 One-month SBI rates have risen more than 100 basis points this year as authorities have tried to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 One big reason for rupiah weakness has been the surge in oil prices. Indonesian demand for oil means extra demand for dollars, and that has resulted in rupiah sales.  \par \par \uc2 For details of the survey and historical SBI rates, Reuters 3000 Xtra users can click on page <BISBIF1> and <BISBI01> respectively.  \par \par \uc2 (With additional reporting by Harry Suhartono)  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-INDONESIA-RATES (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|IF|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050727e17r0014b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
