\par\par \b \uc2 DJ  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  Rupiah Ends Down;Off Lows As Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 177 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juli 2005\par 13:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2005, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The Indonesian rupiah ended lower Thursday as the market tracked a strong dollar, but \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped cushion the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slide, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar closed at 9,805 rupiah, up from IDR9,781 Wednesday. The dollar peaked at IDR9,823 in intraday trading  \par \par \uc2 'We expected the rupiah to go much (lower), but it didn't because Bank Indonesia sold dollars though state banks at the IDR9,820 mark,' a dealer at a foreign bank said.  \par \par \uc2 The release late Wednesday of data showing that the U.S. trade deficit narrowed in May prompted a surge in the U.S. unit against the Japanese yen that local investors tracked with dollar purchases, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 They expect the dollar to range from IDR9,800 to IDR9,820 Friday, with the rupiah likely to gain traction against the greenback from \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . -By Phelim Kyne; Dow Jones Newswires; 62 21 3983 1277; phelim.kyne@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Lena Lee  \par \par \uc2 -0-  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020050714e17e006pp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
