\par\par \b \uc2 Bank Indonesia Chief Says Rupiah Woes To Ease By End '05  \b0\par\par\uc2 352 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juli 2005\par 08:31\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will tackle the current "volatility" in the value of the rupiah and help boost the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to 9,300 against the U.S. dollar by the end of the year, its governor said Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 "In recent months the volatility (in the value) of the rupiah has been higher than usual," Bank Indonesia's Burhanuddin Abdullah told reporters. "We will try to ease that volatility using many policies...(and) if necessary we will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  (in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market)."  \par \par \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  data indicate the rupiah has lost 4.32% in value against the dollar in the past two months.  \par \par \uc2 Burhanuddin'sassertion seems to counter a statement by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Senior Deputy Governor Miranda Gultom, who had said Monday that it is unlikely that the rupiah would go back to the level of IDR9,300 by the end of the year.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar closed at a more-than-three-year high of IDR9,870 on July 5 due to state-owned petroleum firm Pertamina's massive dollar purchases to fund imports at a time when global oil prices hover around $60 a barrel.  \par \par \uc2 The rupiah has since rebounded on the back of a government plan to take Pertamina out of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by directly selling the company dollars through the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . At GMT 0547 Wednesday, the dollar was trading at IDR9,771.  \par \par \uc2 The Pertamina dollar-supply plan is part of a series of rupiah- defense measures the government has announced in recent weeks, including tighter \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rules that will take effect Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 The new rules include a cut in the size of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  derivative transactions with foreign counterparts against the rupiah to a maximum of $1 million from $3 million earlier.  \par \par \uc2 The regulations also limit dollar purchases in outright forward transactions and swaps to a total of $1 million. Such transactions weren't previously subject to any cap.  \par \par \uc2 -By Jakarta Bureau, Dow Jones Newswires; 62 21 3983 1277; dj.jakarta@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Ven Ram [ 13-07-05 0631GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050713e17d0006w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
