\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  Rupiah Ends Up On Talk Of Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 375 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juni 2005\par 12:45\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones Newswires)--The Indonesian rupiah rose Wednesday due to likely market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the U.S. dollar's weakness against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar closed at IDR9,648, down from its close Tuesday at IDR9,665.  \par \par \uc2 The rupiah also benefited from an easing in dollar demand from local corporates, dealers said. Much of that demand was on behalf of state oil importer Pertamina, which is scrambling to comply with a government directive to increase its fuel reserves to cover consumption for 20 days from a current level of 12 days.  \par \par \uc2 "Basically, today was a quiet trading day compared to yesterday's volatility, but again the dollar demand for local corporates is still healthy for the same reason of importing oil," a dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 "Also, we see some dollar-selling by state banks, probably on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  as part of its regulatory role in preventing the dollar from rising too fast (against the rupiah)."  \par \par \uc2 The dollar's weakness against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  also helped the rupiah. The dollar fell to HK$7.7706 Wednesday from HK$7.7743 Tuesday due to renewed speculation about a possible revaluation of the Chinese yuan. Against the New Taiwan dollar, the U.S. dollar closed at NT$31.355, down from NT$31.390 Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Indonesia's looming implementation of tighter \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading rules has also severely trimmed speculative trading in the rupiah, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia will implement next month regulations that will restrict the amount of dollars banks can borrow from offshore counterparts without underlying transactions at $1 million. Previously, there was no cap on the amount.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials have said that the move is aimed at reducing the amount of speculative offshore money coming into Indonesia, which can destabilize the exchange rate.  \par \par \uc2 "Domestic flow is the main driver (of dollar demand)," a dealer said. "Since the regulations came out, I think speculative flows have very much reduced."  \par \par \uc2 Dealers expect the dollar to trade between IDR9,630 and IDR9,680 Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 -By Phelim Kyne; Dow Jones Newswires' Jakarta Bureau; 62 21 3983 1277; phelim.kyne@dowjones.com [ 22-06-05 1045GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1159 1848  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050622e16m000j9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
