\par\par \b \uc2 CORRECTED - CORRECTED-UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  c.bank sees rupiah  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  tem  \b0\par\par\uc2 252 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juni 2005\par 08:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 In the JAKARTA story headlined "UPDATE 1-\b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  c.bank sees rupiah \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  temporary" please read in third paragraph ... net oil exporter ... instead of ... net oil importer ... (corrects word).  \par \par \uc2 A corrected story follows.  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, June 8 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor said on Wednesday that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to help the rupiah \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <IDR=> was a temporary solution.  \par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is only for a short term. We cannot stay like this. We need to keep the economy in balance to solve this problem," Burhanuddin Abdullah said at an Indonesian Chamber of Commerce meeting.  \par \par \uc2 Abdullah added that becoming a net oil exporter once again would be an important goal in trying to maintain balance in the economy.  \par \par \uc2 "An increase in the oil price should benefit the Indonesian economy if we are a net exporter. That's what we should achieve. Without it we will be very vulnerable".  \par \par \uc2 Despite being the only Asian member of Organisation of Petroleum Exporting Countries, Indonesia has been a net oil importer during recent periods.  \par \par \uc2 Sharp increases in oil prices also weigh on the state budget as Jakarta subsidises the domestic fuel price.  \par \par \uc2 The cost for this subsidy was expected to reach 76.5 trillion rupiah ($7.98 billion) this year, according to the revised state budget, up from 19 trillion forecasted earlier. ($1=9,590 rupiah)  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-INDONESIA-RUPIAH (UPDATE 1, CORRECTION)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|IF|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050608e16800064\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
