\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Indonesia Rupiah Ends Flat On Alleged Central Bk Moves  \b0\par\par\uc2 212 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Mai 2005\par 12:24\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2005, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The Indonesian rupiah closed steady Monday thanks to reported \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the dollar's rebound versus major rivals from spilling over to the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar closed at IDR9,480, unchanged from its close Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the greenback rose to an intraday high of IDR9,510 earlier in the day, which triggered alleged dollar selling by the nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 'Some foreigners sold dollars during the afternoon session, likely because after they saw the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's resolve in defending the rupiah,' a dealer with an international bank said.  \par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia has been reported to have sold dollars almost every day in the last three weeks after the rupiah fell to three-year lows last month.  \par \par \uc2 Helping the rupiah recoup its lost ground is crucial in helping reduce upward pressure on the inflation.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers expect the dollar to trade between IDR9,460 and IDR9,500 Tuesday, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  expected to unload dollars to keep the U.S. unit below the psychologically-important IDR9,500 level. -By I Made Sentana; Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277; I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Paul Baylis  \par \par \uc2 -0-  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020050509e159005sh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\p