\par\par \b \uc2 Indonesia Rupiah Ends Higher; Suspected Ctrl Bk Dlr Sales  \b0\par\par\uc2 200 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Mai 2005\par 11:55\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The Indonesian rupiah closed higher Friday following suspected sales of dollars by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help the local unit regain lost ground against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar closed at 9,480 rupiah, down from IDR9,505 Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Indonesia's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was closed Thursday for a public holiday.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said market players liquidated their dollar-long positions from the start of trading, dragging the U.S. unit down to an intraday low of IDR9,475 early in the session.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar's rebound against the yen sparked fresh dollar-rupiah bids, but the U.S. unit's recovery was cut short by Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Trading volume was relatively thin as many market participants chose to stay on the sidelines ahead of the weekend, they said.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers expect the dollar to trade between IDR9,420 and IDR9,500 Monday, with dollar/yen movements providing direction for trading in Jakarta's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 -By I Made Sentana; Dow Jones Newswires; 62-21 39831277; I-Made.Sentana@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Lena Lee [ 06-05-05 0955GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 1159 1848  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050506e156000gh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
