\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  rph up on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 , lower dlr demand.  \b0\par\par\uc2 220 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Mai 2005\par 07:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, May 2 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah strengthened slightly on Monday partly on an easing of dollar demand from local corporates and a suspected small amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the thin market.  \par \par \uc2 The rupiah was quoted at 9,530/9,540 per dollar at 0520 GMT, up from 9,585 late on Friday, when it fell as much as 0.6 percent despite a sharp rise in other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on heightened speculation that China would revalue the yuan soon.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , that has helped the rupiah to strengthen. Apart from that, Pertamina is not seen buying dollars in the market today," said a dealer with a private bank in Jakarta.  \par \par \uc2 Last week the Indonesian authorities announced various money market measures to soak up excess rupiah in the system, promised higher interest rates and raised guaranteed deposit rates sharply.  \par \par \uc2 But the boost from these efforts proved limited and the rupiah headed lower after recovering by 3 percent between April 26 and 28.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts have said the rupiah would probably remain under pressure as long as state oil firm Pertamina continues to buy dollars from the market to import oil and unless investors regain their confidence in Indonesia's monetary policy and economic growth prospects.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050502e152004s9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
