\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Rupiah jumps on govt moves, peso up on China.  \b0\par\par\uc2 626 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 April 2005\par 12:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Yoo Choonsik\par     SINGAPORE, April 27 (Reuters) - Indonesian efforts to shore\par up the rupiah drove the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  more than 1 percent higher on\par Wednesday, while a weak Philippine peso found support from\par Chinese investment and lending plans.\par     The peso was quoted at 54.36 per dollar late on Wednesday,\par against 54.35 on Tuesday, having slipped as low as 54.60\par earlier.\par     However, it climbed from the intraday lows after China's\par president, Hu Jintao, agreed China would invest and loan $1.6\par billion to fund infrastructure and mining projects in the\par Philippines.\par     The South Korean won ended domestic trade 0.1 percent\par lower, marking its first drop in eight sessions. The Singapore\par and Taiwan dollar were slightly weaker as the U.S. dollar rose\par following strong data on new home sales.\par     The rupiah gained as much as 1.1 percent to 9,585 per\par dollar, bouncing from three-year lows generated by concern\par Indonesia's monetary policy was too loose.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has lost 3.4 percent so far this year making\par it Asia's weakest actively traded \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after the Japanese\par yen.\par     Some analysts doubted the rupiah had secured a turnaround,\par pointing to high oil prices, investor concern over economic\par prospects and signs investors are moving out of emerging market\par debt as U.S. interest rates rise.\par     "I would say it will provide some relief, but ultimately\par (the rupiah) will still be subject to a combination of\par factors," said Philip Wee, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist with DBS Bank.\par     This week, Indonesian officials have promised higher\par interest rates. Indonesia introduced a new short-term money\par market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and promised more frequent auctions of debt to\par absorb excess rupiah.\par     Officials also considered on Wednesday measures to allow\par state oil firm Pertamina to buy dollars from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par instead of from the market to pay for oil imports.\par     But late in the day State Enterprises Minister Sugiharto,\par who oversees Pertamina, said the company would continue to buy\par dollars from the market, purchases dealers have cited as\par weakening the rupiah.\par  \par     Sugiharto said Pertamina needed about $50 million each day,\par suggesting its monthly demand could amount to some $1 billion.\par    Indonesian President Susilo Bambang Yudhoyono ordered\par officials to seek ways to stabilise rupiah and dealers also\par cited some dollar-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by authorities.\par     "Though the BI (Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) remains on guard to prevent\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the dollar/rupiah from hitting 10,000, much will still depend  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 on the development of oil prices and dollar movements," Chin  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Loo Thio, a senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analyst with BNP Paribas, said in a  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 research report.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We expect choppy trade between 9,500 to 9,800 (rupiah per  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dollar)." \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Change on the day at 0800 GMT   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       106.17         105.89       -0.26\par  Sing dlr        1.6480         1.6467       -0.08\par  Taiwan dlr      31.439         31.413       -0.08\par  Korean won     1002.70        0998.90       -0.38\par  Baht             39.56          39.45       -0.28\par  Peso             54.36          54.35       -0.02\par  Rupiah         9612.00        9690.00       +0.81\par  Rupee            43.70          43.66       -0.09\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       106.17         102.45       -3.50\par  Sing dlr        1.6480         1.6310       -1.03\par  Taiwan dlr      31.439         31.920       +1.53\par  Korean won     1002.70        1035.10       +3.23\par  Baht             39.56          38.88       -1.72\par  Peso             54.36          56.28       +3.53\par  Rupiah         9612.00        9290.00       -3.35\par  Rupee            43.70          43.47       -0.53\par  ------------------------------------------------- ((Editing by\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Neil Fullick; choonsik.yoo@reuters.com; Reuters Messaging:  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 choonsik.yoo.reuters.com@reuters.net; +65 6870 3925)).  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050427e14r007sq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
